{
  "name": "Generate Veo 3.1 videos and Nano Banana Pro images from a form with Google Flow",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "name": "Prompt form",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.formTrigger",
      "position": [
        0,
        300
      ],
      "webhookId": "b6f1c7e2-3d4a-4f5b-9c8d-1e2f3a4b5c6d",
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "formTitle": "Google Flow: Veo 3.1 video or Nano Banana Pro image",
        "formFields": {
          "values": [
            {
              "fieldType": "textarea",
              "fieldLabel": "Prompt",
              "requiredField": true
            },
            {
              "fieldType": "dropdown",
              "fieldLabel": "Type",
              "fieldOptions": {
                "values": [
                  {
                    "option": "Image"
                  },
                  {
                    "option": "Video"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "requiredField": true
            },
            {
              "fieldType": "dropdown",
              "fieldLabel": "Orientation",
              "fieldOptions": {
                "values": [
                  {
                    "option": "Landscape"
                  },
                  {
                    "option": "Portrait"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "requiredField": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "formDescription": "Generates on your own Google Flow account through the useapi.net API."
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "name": "Settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        240,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "a1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.Prompt }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "a2",
              "name": "type",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.Type }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "a3",
              "name": "orientation",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.Orientation }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "a4",
              "name": "imageModel",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "nano-banana-pro"
            },
            {
              "id": "a5",
              "name": "videoModel",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "veo-3.1-fast"
            },
            {
              "id": "a6",
              "name": "count",
              "type": "number",
              "value": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "a7",
              "name": "email",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "name": "Image or video?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
        480,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 2,
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.type }}",
              "rightValue": "Image"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "name": "Generate images",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "maxTries": 3,
      "position": [
        720,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://api.useapi.net/v1/google-flow/images",
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 180000
        },
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify(Object.assign({ prompt: $json.prompt, model: $json.imageModel, aspectRatio: $json.orientation === 'Portrait' ? '9:16' : '16:9', count: $json.count }, $json.email ? { email: $json.email } : {})) }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth"
      },
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "id": "useapiHeaderAuth",
          "name": "useapi.net API token"
        }
      },
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000
    },
    {
      "name": "Images to files",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        960,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Each image comes back as a signed fifeUrl, or inline as base64 when the URL is missing\nconst out = []\nfor (const [i, m] of ($input.first().json.media ?? []).entries()) {\n  const img = m.image?.generatedImage ?? {}\n  const fileName = `nano-banana-${i + 1}.jpg`\n  const buffer = img.fifeUrl\n    ? Buffer.from(await this.helpers.httpRequest({ url: img.fifeUrl, encoding: 'arraybuffer', json: false }))\n    : Buffer.from(img.encodedImage ?? m.encodedImage ?? '', 'base64')\n  out.push({\n    json: { mediaGenerationId: img.mediaGenerationId, fileName },\n    binary: { data: await this.helpers.prepareBinaryData(buffer, fileName, 'image/jpeg') },\n  })\n}\nreturn out"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Start video job",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "maxTries": 3,
      "position": [
        720,
        460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://api.useapi.net/v1/google-flow/videos",
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 180000
        },
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify(Object.assign({ prompt: $json.prompt, model: $json.videoModel, aspectRatio: $json.orientation === 'Portrait' ? 'portrait' : 'landscape', count: $json.count, async: true }, $json.email ? { email: $json.email } : {})) }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth"
      },
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "id": "useapiHeaderAuth",
          "name": "useapi.net API token"
        }
      },
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000
    },
    {
      "name": "Wait 20s",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.wait",
      "position": [
        960,
        460
      ],
      "webhookId": "c7a2d8f3-4e5b-4a6c-8d9e-2f3a4b5c6d7e",
      "parameters": {
        "amount": 20
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.1
    },
    {
      "name": "Check job",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "maxTries": 3,
      "position": [
        1200,
        460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ 'https://api.useapi.net/v1/google-flow/jobs/' + $('Start video job').item.json.jobid }}",
        "method": "GET",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 60000
        },
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth"
      },
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "id": "useapiHeaderAuth",
          "name": "useapi.net API token"
        }
      },
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000
    },
    {
      "name": "Job status",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.switch",
      "position": [
        1440,
        460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rules": {
          "values": [
            {
              "outputKey": "completed",
              "conditions": {
                "options": {
                  "version": 2,
                  "leftValue": "",
                  "caseSensitive": true,
                  "typeValidation": "strict"
                },
                "combinator": "and",
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "operator": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "operation": "equals"
                    },
                    "leftValue": "={{ $json.status }}",
                    "rightValue": "completed"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "renameOutput": true
            },
            {
              "outputKey": "failed",
              "conditions": {
                "options": {
                  "version": 2,
                  "leftValue": "",
                  "caseSensitive": true,
                  "typeValidation": "strict"
                },
                "combinator": "and",
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "operator": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "operation": "equals"
                    },
                    "leftValue": "={{ $json.status }}",
                    "rightValue": "failed"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "renameOutput": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "fallbackOutput": "extra",
          "renameFallbackOutput": "still running"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.2
    },
    {
      "name": "Videos to files",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        1680,
        360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// A job with count > 1 returns several videos, each as a signed videoUrl\nconst out = []\nfor (const [i, m] of ($input.first().json.response?.media ?? []).entries()) {\n  const fileName = `veo-${i + 1}.mp4`\n  const buffer = Buffer.from(await this.helpers.httpRequest({ url: m.videoUrl, encoding: 'arraybuffer', json: false }))\n  out.push({\n    json: { mediaGenerationId: m.mediaGenerationId, fileName },\n    binary: { data: await this.helpers.prepareBinaryData(buffer, fileName, 'video/mp4') },\n  })\n}\nreturn out"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Job failed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stopAndError",
      "position": [
        1680,
        560
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "errorMessage": "={{ 'Google Flow job failed: ' + ($json.error ?? 'no reason given') }}"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -460,
        -40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 420,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "## Generate Veo 3.1 videos and Nano Banana Pro images from a form with Google Flow\n\nTurn a prompt into a **Veo 3.1** video or a **Nano Banana Pro** image on your own Google Flow account, and get the finished file back as binary data ready for the next node.\n\n### Who's it for\nContent creators, marketers and automation builders who already pay for a Google AI plan and want Flow's models inside n8n, without metered Gemini API billing per clip or image.\n\n### How it works\n1. A form collects the prompt, the output type (image or video) and the orientation.\n2. **Images:** one synchronous request to the [useapi.net Google Flow API](https://useapi.net/docs/api-google-flow-v1) returns the images, which a Code node saves from their signed URLs.\n3. **Video:** the workflow starts an async job, waits, checks the job, and loops until it is completed or failed, then downloads the MP4.\n\n### How to set up\n1. Create a useapi.net account and [API token](https://useapi.net/docs/start-here/setup-useapi), then connect your Google account with the [automated setup](https://useapi.net/docs/start-here/setup-google-flow).\n2. Create a **Header Auth** credential. Name: `Authorization`. Value: `Bearer <your API token>`.\n3. Select the credential on the three HTTP Request nodes.\n4. Open the form URL (or click **Test workflow**) and submit a prompt.\n\n### Requirements\n- A useapi.net subscription ($15/month flat, covers 3 Google Flow accounts).\n- A Google account. Images work on any Google AI plan, including a free one. Video needs a paid plan and spends its Flow credits.\n\n### How to customize\n- Change the models and the number of results in the **Settings** node, including `omni-flash` (Omni 1.1 Flash: audio-native video with voices, available only in Google Flow).\n- Swap the form for a Schedule, Google Sheets or Airtable trigger to generate in batches.\n- Add a Google Drive, S3 or Telegram node after the last Code nodes to deliver the files."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Settings note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        180,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 220,
        "height": 220,
        "content": "### Settings\nChange the models here. Image: `nano-banana-pro`, `nano-banana-2`, `nano-banana-2-lite`. Video: `veo-3.1-fast`, `veo-3.1-lite`, `veo-3.1-quality`, `omni-flash`. Leave `email` empty unless you connect several Google accounts and want a specific one."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Images note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        660,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 520,
        "height": 180,
        "content": "### Images\nOne synchronous call, usually 10\u201320 seconds. The Code node saves each image from its signed URL, or from inline base64 when the URL is missing."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Video note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        660,
        640
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1000,
        "height": 160,
        "content": "### Video\nVideo is asynchronous: start the job, wait, check it, and loop until it is `completed` or `failed`. A Veo 3.1 Fast clip usually takes 1\u20133 minutes. Signed video URLs expire, so download them right away, which the last Code node does."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
  "pinData": {},
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1"
  },
